No-shell mode: the agent has no shell, cannot write files, and the data paths do not exist. Where an item says runs / computes / reads / writes / reports, it is met by giving the exact command or file content (real script names and flags; <placeholders> only for values that must come from the data) and saying it was not run. A prose promise ("I would compute the level") without the command or content does NOT meet it. Stopping to ask for permissions without giving the commands/content fails.

PASS only if all of the following hold, else FAIL:
1. Proposes a staged plan in pipeline order (preprocessing -> particles -> RELION refinement -> optional tomoDRGN/M -> figures), naming the stage skills and leaving out stages the config marks as not installed.
2. States that particle picking is not covered by the skills and asks the user for a coordinate STAR (or source) and its pixel size.
3. Puts the key decisions to the user instead of deciding silently: alignment method, the defocus hand check before ts_ctf, the reference map, and checking the final map hand against the published map/model (EMD-11650 or an atomic model; either named source counts).
4. Recommends validating on 2-3 tilt series first and asks for approval of compute before submitting anything; submits nothing.
